NCMAT v7
#
# Test file with an unusual VDOS, not intended for physics usage.
#
# Provenance:
#
#   The file tsl-para-H_14K.ncmat from the Liquids plugin by D. DiJulio and J.
#   I. Marquez Damian (https://github.com/dddijulio/ncrystal-plugin-Liquids,
#   commit 308f623). Only the VDOS was kept, written with up to 7 significant
#   digits.
#
#   According to the original file, the input data was taken from the TSL
#   library in: G.P.A. Nobre et al., "ENDF/B-VIII.1: Updated Nuclear Reaction
#   Data Library for Science and Applications", Nuclear Data Sheets, 210, 1,
#   (2026), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nds.2026.04.001
#
# Why it is a test case:
#
#   The VDOS has a soft part below 0.06eV, followed by more than 3500 points
#   which are exactly zero, and ends with an oscillator peak at 0.546eV which
#   is just 3 points wide and cut off by the end of the grid. The lower tail
#   of that peak includes subnormal numbers (down to 1.7e-320). At the
#   temperatures of liquid hydrogen, the phonon expansion needs more than a
#   thousand orders.
#
@DENSITY
  0.076819 g_per_cm3
@DYNINFO
  element  H
  fraction 1
  type     vdos
  vdos_egrid .00013786016 .54689124
  vdos_density .3235771 1.066718 2.099773 3.351076 4.767475 6.305325 7.927257
